{
  "about": "The range a number typed into an advanced field (an override) may take, per kind and dotted path; * matches any one step (a list position or a key). A field not listed and at or above zero cannot go negative; a negative one may take either sign. Either way it stays within 1000 times its size (1000 when it is 0 or small). An \"auto\" field (null in the data) takes nothing or a number in its range. Sizes a bench divides by start above zero, and the test settings that decide how many frames a run computes keep a run under about 20 seconds on the owner's laptop (the default settings take under one). text says which text fields may change: refs are the kinds whose ids other items point at (a field holding one is a pick of that kind), choices the fixed answers of a field, free the fields that only describe (at most max_chars characters), fixed the fields that hold an id yet are no pick (an actuator's kind decides how it is built; nothing reads the girdle's joint). Any other text decides how an item is built and is fixed.",
